IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `fca4a-rules`

-- Federal Court of Australia Act 1976 (Cth), Part IVA -- the questions of the claimant in a class action: a group member,
-- or a person with a claim who starts or runs a class action as the representative party.
--
-- Based on content from the Federal Register of Legislation: "Federal Court of Australia Act 1976", Compilation No. 59
-- (11 December 2024), and "Federal Court Rules 2011", Compilation No. 11 (11 June 2026), Commonwealth of Australia,
-- licensed under CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as
-- advice. See NOTES.md.
--
-- Every question takes plain facts only. What the Court decides (whether it is satisfied, thinks it just, finds an issue
-- common) is asked as a fact: "if the Court ...". A yes about the Court means the Court can do it, not that it will.

§ `Federal Court of Australia Act 1976 Part IVA -- my questions in a class action`

§§ `Can my claim be in a class action? (ss 33B, 33C, 33D, 33G)`

@export Can my claim be brought in a class action (a "representative proceeding") in the Federal Court of Australia under Part IVA of the Federal Court of Australia Act 1976 (ss 33B, 33C, 33G)? Needs 7 or more people with claims against the same person, arising from the same, similar or related circumstances, with a substantial common issue, on a cause of action arising on or after 4 March 1992.
GIVEN `the day my claim arose` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your cause of action arise (ISO date, e.g. 2025-03-15)?
      `how many of us have claims` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people, counting you, have claims against the same person (company, government or individual)?
      `our claims share circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do all the claims arise out of, or concern, the same, similar or related circumstances?
      `our claims share a substantial issue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do all the claims raise a substantial common issue of law or fact (for example whether the product was defective or the statement misleading)?
      `the Court's only jurisdiction is cross-vesting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the Federal Court have jurisdiction over every claim only because of the cross-vesting laws (Jurisdiction of Courts (Cross-vesting) Act 1987 or a State or Territory equivalent)? Answer no if unsure or if the claims are under a Commonwealth law.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can my claim be brought in a class action?` `the day my claim arose` `how many of us have claims` `our claims share circumstances` `our claims share a substantial issue` `the Court's only jurisdiction is cross-vesting` MEANS
    `s 33C -- the claims can be brought as a representative proceeding` `the day my claim arose` `how many of us have claims` `our claims share circumstances` `our claims share a substantial issue` `the Court's only jurisdiction is cross-vesting`

@export Can I start the class action myself, as the representative party, for the others with claims (ss 33C, 33D(1) of the Federal Court of Australia Act 1976)? Not answered where you could not sue on your own behalf, which the Act does not settle.
GIVEN `the day my claim arose` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your cause of action arise (ISO date)?
      `how many of us have claims` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people, counting you, have claims against the same person?
      `our claims share circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do all the claims arise out of the same, similar or related circumstances?
      `our claims share a substantial issue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do all the claims raise a substantial common issue of law or fact?
      `the Court's only jurisdiction is cross-vesting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the Federal Court have jurisdiction over every claim only because of the cross-vesting laws?
      `I could sue on my own` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a sufficient interest to sue that person on your own behalf (normally yes, if you have a claim against them yourself)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I start the class action as representative party?` `the day my claim arose` `how many of us have claims` `our claims share circumstances` `our claims share a substantial issue` `the Court's only jurisdiction is cross-vesting` `I could sue on my own` MEANS
    `both`
        (`s 33C -- the claims can be brought as a representative proceeding` `the day my claim arose` `how many of us have claims` `our claims share circumstances` `our claims share a substantial issue` `the Court's only jurisdiction is cross-vesting`)
        (`s 33D(1) -- I have standing to commence` `I could sue on my own`)

-- Situation: only for the person who started the class action.
@export If I started the class action, can I keep running it and appeal from its judgment even after my own claim against the respondent ends, for example because I settled (s 33D(2) of the Federal Court of Australia Act 1976)?
GIVEN `I started it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you commence the class action (are you the representative party who started it)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I keep running the class action without a claim of my own?` `I started it` MEANS
    `s 33D(2) -- I keep my standing without a claim` `I started it`

§§ `Am I in the group? (ss 33A, 33E, 33F)`

@export Am I a group member in this class action (ss 33A, 33E of the Federal Court of Australia Act 1976)? An individual or company described in the group is in it without consenting; the Commonwealth, a State or Territory, a Minister, a public-purpose statutory body or an official acting as such is in only with written consent (Form 20).
GIVEN `the group described includes me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the description of the group in the originating application (or as amended) cover you? You need not be named.
      `what I am` IS A `Kind of person` @desc Which are you? Most people and companies choose "an individual or a company or other person not listed".
      `I consented in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you given written consent to be a group member (Federal Court Rules form 20)? Only matters for the government bodies and officials listed.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Am I a group member?` `the group described includes me` `what I am` `I consented in writing` MEANS
    `ss 33A, 33E -- I am a group member` `the group described includes me` `what I am` `I consented in writing`

@export Do I have to consent to be a group member in a class action (s 33E of the Federal Court of Australia Act 1976)? Only the Commonwealth, a State or Territory, a Minister, a public-purpose statutory body or an official acting as such must consent, in writing.
GIVEN `what I am` IS A `Kind of person` @desc Which are you? Most people and companies choose "an individual or a company or other person not listed".
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Must I consent to be a group member?` `what I am` MEANS
    `s 33E(2) -- consent in writing is needed` `what I am`

-- Situation: only for a group member under a legal disability (a child, or a person who cannot manage their affairs).
@export Do I need a next friend or committee (a litigation representative) to be a group member, or to take a step in the class action myself, while I am under a legal disability (s 33F of the Federal Court of Australia Act 1976)?
GIVEN `I am under disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you under a legal disability (for example a child, or a person who cannot manage their own affairs in the proceeding)?
      `what I want to do` IS A `What I want to do` @desc Do you just want to be a group member, or to take a step in the proceeding or conduct part of it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Do I need a next friend or committee?` `I am under disability` `what I want to do` MEANS
    `s 33F -- I need a next friend or committee` `I am under disability` `what I want to do`

§§ `Opting out (ss 33J, 33ZB, 33ZC(8))`

@export Can I opt out of the class action by giving notice on this day (s 33J of the Federal Court of Australia Act 1976, Federal Court Rules 2011 r 9.34)? The notice must be written, in Form 21, and given before the opt-out date the Court fixed: on that date itself is too late. There is no opt-out from an appeal.
GIVEN `the opt-out date` IS A DATE @desc What is the opt-out date the Court fixed (or extended to) in the notice you received (ISO date)? Notice must be given before it.
      `the day I give notice` IS A DATE @desc On what day will you give (or did you give) your opt-out notice (ISO date)?
      `my notice is written in Form 21` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your notice in writing, in Form 21 of the Federal Court Rules?
      `this is an appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proceeding you want to leave an appeal from the class action's judgment, rather than the class action itself?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I opt out of the class action?` `the opt-out date` `the day I give notice` `my notice is written in Form 21` `this is an appeal` MEANS
    `s 33J(2) -- I can opt out` `the opt-out date` `the day I give notice` `my notice is written in Form 21` `this is an appeal`

@export What is the last day I can give my opt-out notice in the class action (s 33J(2) of the Federal Court of Australia Act 1976)? The day before the opt-out date the Court fixed, since notice must be given "before" that date.
GIVEN `the opt-out date` IS A DATE @desc What is the opt-out date the Court fixed (or extended to) (ISO date)?
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I opt out?` `the opt-out date` MEANS
    `s 33J(2) -- the last day to opt out` `the opt-out date`

@export Can the hearing of the class action start on this day, before I have had the chance to opt out (s 33J(4) of the Federal Court of Australia Act 1976)? Not earlier than the opt-out date, unless the Court gives leave.
GIVEN `the hearing day` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the hearing to start (ISO date)?
      `the opt-out date` IS A DATE @desc What is the opt-out date the Court fixed (ISO date)?
      `the Court gave leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court given leave for the hearing to start earlier?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the hearing start before my opt-out date?` `the hearing day` `the opt-out date` `the Court gave leave` MEANS
    `s 33J(4) -- the hearing can start then` `the hearing day` `the opt-out date` `the Court gave leave`

@export Will the class action's judgment bind me (s 33ZB of the Federal Court of Australia Act 1976)? It binds every group member it describes, except anyone who opted out under s 33J.
GIVEN `the judgment describes me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the judgment describe or identify you among the group members it affects?
      `I opted out` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you opt out of the class action under s 33J?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Will the judgment bind me?` `the judgment describes me` `I opted out` MEANS
    `s 33ZB -- the judgment binds me` `the judgment describes me` `I opted out`

-- Situation: only where the claimant's cause of action arose after the class action started.
@export My claim arose after the class action started. Can the group be widened to take me in (s 33K of the Federal Court of Australia Act 1976)? Only on the representative party's application with the Court's leave; your claim must have arisen before the date the Court fixes, and you must be someone who would have been in the group had it arisen earlier.
GIVEN `the day my claim arose` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your cause of action accrue (ISO date)?
      `the day the class action began` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the class action commenced (ISO date)?
      `the date the Court fixes` IS A DATE @desc What cut-off date did (or would) the Court fix when giving leave (ISO date)? Claims must accrue before it.
      `I would have been in the group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you have been in the group (with your consent, where needed) if your claim had arisen before the class action began?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the group be widened to include my later claim?` `the day my claim arose` `the day the class action began` `the date the Court fixes` `I would have been in the group` MEANS
    `s 33K -- the group can be altered to include me` `the day my claim arose` `the day the class action began` `the date the Court fixes` `I would have been in the group`

§§ `My time limit (s 33ZE)`

@export What happens to the time limit (limitation period) for my own claim while I am in the class action (s 33ZE of the Federal Court of Australia Act 1976)? It stops running when the class action starts and runs again only if I opt out, or the class action and its appeals end without finally deciding my claim; this gives the new last day.
GIVEN `my claim is in the class action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim one of the group members' claims the class action is about?
      `my old last day` IS A DATE @desc What was the last day to sue on your claim under the limitation law that applies, before the class action (ISO date)?
      `the day the class action began` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the class action commenced (ISO date)?
      `where my claim stands` IS A `Where my claim stands` @desc Is the class action still going, did you opt out, did it (and its appeals) end without finally deciding your claim, or was your claim finally decided in it?
      `the day that happened` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you opt out, or did the class action and its appeals end (ISO date)? Ignored if it is still going.
GIVETH A `Limitation answer`
`What happens to my time limit?` `my claim is in the class action` `my old last day` `the day the class action began` `where my claim stands` `the day that happened` MEANS
    `s 33ZE -- my limitation period` `my claim is in the class action` `my old last day` `the day the class action began` `where my claim stands` `the day that happened`

§§ `Notices (ss 33X, 33Y(8))`

@export Must I, as a group member, be given notice of this in the class action (s 33X of the Federal Court of Australia Act 1976)? Notice must be given as soon as practicable after the event, in the form and way the Court approves.
GIVEN `what it is about` IS A `What the notice is about` @desc What is the notice about?
      `damages are claimed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the class action claim damages?
      `the Court dispensed with notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court dispensed with giving this notice?
      `the Court ordered notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court ordered that notice of it be given to group members?
      `the Court thinks it just to go ahead without notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a settlement: is the Court satisfied it is just to decide the approval application without notice to group members?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must I be given notice of this?` `what it is about` `damages are claimed` `the Court dispensed with notice` `the Court ordered notice` `the Court thinks it just to go ahead without notice` MEANS
    `s 33X -- I must be given notice` `what it is about` `damages are claimed` `the Court dispensed with notice` `the Court ordered notice` `the Court thinks it just to go ahead without notice`

@export If I did not receive, or did not respond to, a notice in the class action, does that undo a step taken, an order made or a judgment given (s 33Y(8) of the Federal Court of Australia Act 1976)? No.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does missing a notice affect the class action?` MEANS
    `s 33Y(8) -- missing a notice affects the proceeding`

§§ `The representative party (ss 33T, 33W)`

@export Can the Court replace the representative party on my application as a group member (or sub-group member) because they cannot adequately represent us (s 33T of the Federal Court of Australia Act 1976)?
GIVEN `the Court finds them inadequate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the Court that the representative party (or sub-group representative party) cannot adequately represent the group's (or sub-group's) interests?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the representative party be replaced?` `the Court finds them inadequate` MEANS
    `s 33T -- the representative can be replaced on my application` `the Court finds them inadequate`

@export Can the representative party be given leave to withdraw from the class action (s 33W(4) of the Federal Court of Australia Act 1976)? Only after group members have been told in time to apply for a substitute, and any such application has been decided.
GIVEN `group members were told in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Court satisfied that group members were given notice of the withdrawal application (under s 33X(1)) in time to apply for another representative?
      `substitution applications are decided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has every application to substitute another group member as representative been decided (answer yes if there was none)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the representative party withdraw?` `group members were told in time` `substitution applications are decided` MEANS
    `s 33W(4) -- the representative can be let withdraw` `group members were told in time` `substitution applications are decided`

§§ `If it stops being a class action (ss 33L, 33M, 33N, 33P)`

@export Can the Court order that the class action no longer continue as a class action (ss 33L, 33M, 33N of the Federal Court of Australia Act 1976)? If the Court thinks there are likely fewer than 7 group members, or (where money is claimed for group members) finds identifying and paying them would cost too much, or is satisfied it is in the interests of justice on a s 33N ground.
GIVEN `group members the Court thinks likely` IS A NUMBER @desc How many group members does it appear likely to the Court there are?
      `money is claimed for group members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the class action claim payment of money to group members (other than costs)?
      `the Court finds paying us would cost too much` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On the respondent's application, has the Court concluded that identifying group members and paying them would likely cost the respondent too much compared with the likely total?
      `the Court is satisfied under s 33N` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Court satisfied it is in the interests of justice to stop, because separate cases would cost less, other proceedings could get all the relief, the class action would not be efficient and effective, or it is otherwise inappropriate?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the class action be stopped?` `group members the Court thinks likely` `money is claimed for group members` `the Court finds paying us would cost too much` `the Court is satisfied under s 33N` MEANS
    `ss 33L, 33M, 33N -- the Court can stop the class action` `group members the Court thinks likely` `money is claimed for group members` `the Court finds paying us would cost too much` `the Court is satisfied under s 33N`

-- Situation: only after an order that the proceeding no longer continue as a class action.
@export If the Court ordered that the class action no longer continue as one, can I still pursue my own claim in that proceeding (s 33P of the Federal Court of Australia Act 1976)? The representative party may continue it for themselves; a group member may apply to be joined as an applicant, which the Court may order.
GIVEN `the Court ordered it stop` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court ordered under s 33L, 33M or 33N that the proceeding no longer continue as a class action?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I go on with my own claim after the class action stops?` `the Court ordered it stop` MEANS
    `s 33P -- I can go on with my own claim in it` `the Court ordered it stop`

§§ `Costs (s 43(1A), ss 33Q, 33R, 33ZJ)`

@export Can the Court order me to pay these costs in the class action (s 43(1A), ss 33Q(3), 33R(2) of the Federal Court of Australia Act 1976)? A group member who is not a party cannot be ordered to pay costs, except the costs of an issue about their own claim they were allowed to argue, or as a sub-group representative.
GIVEN `my part` IS A `My part in the class action` @desc What is your part in the class action?
      `which costs` IS A `Kind of costs` @desc Which costs are you asking about?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I be ordered to pay costs?` `my part` `which costs` MEANS
    `s 43(1A) -- costs can be awarded against me` `my part` `which costs`

@export What is the most of the damages awarded in the class action that the Court can order paid to the representative party to cover their costs (s 33ZJ of the Federal Court of Australia Act 1976)? Up to the amount by which their reasonable costs exceed what they can recover from the respondent, and never more than the damages; 0 if there is no award or no application.
GIVEN `damages were awarded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court awarded damages in the class action?
      `the representative applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the representative party (or a sub-group representative, or a former one) applied under s 33ZJ?
      `their reasonable costs` IS A NUMBER @desc In dollars: the costs the Court accepts the applicant reasonably incurred in the class action.
      `their recoverable costs` IS A NUMBER @desc In dollars: the costs the Court thinks the applicant is likely to recover from the respondent.
      `the damages` IS A NUMBER @desc In dollars: the damages awarded.
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`How much of the damages can go to the representative's costs?` `damages were awarded` `the representative applied` `their reasonable costs` `their recoverable costs` `the damages` MEANS
    `s 33ZJ -- the most paid to the representative out of the damages` `damages were awarded` `the representative applied` `their reasonable costs` `their recoverable costs` `the damages`

§§ `Settlement, judgment and payment (ss 33U, 33V, 33Z, 33ZA, 33ZH)`

@export Can the class action I am in be settled or discontinued (s 33V, s 33X(4) of the Federal Court of Australia Act 1976)? Only with the Court's approval, and the Court must not decide the approval without notice to group members unless it is satisfied that is just.
GIVEN `the Court approves` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does (or did) the Court approve the settlement or discontinuance?
      `group members were told` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were group members given notice of the application for approval?
      `the Court thinks it just to go ahead without notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Court satisfied it is just to decide the application without notice to group members?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the class action be settled?` `the Court approves` `group members were told` `the Court thinks it just to go ahead without notice` MEANS
    `ss 33V, 33X(4) -- the class action can be settled` `the Court approves` `group members were told` `the Court thinks it just to go ahead without notice`

@export Can the Court award the group's damages as one lump sum without fixing my share (s 33Z(1)(f), (3) of the Federal Court of Australia Act 1976)? Only if a reasonably accurate assessment of the group's total entitlement can be made; under a settlement the Act does not say.
GIVEN `this is a settlement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the award made under a settlement the Court approves?
      `the total can be assessed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can a reasonably accurate assessment be made of the total amount group members will be entitled to?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can damages be awarded as a lump sum?` `this is a settlement` `the total can be assessed` MEANS
    `s 33Z(3) -- damages can be awarded as a lump sum` `this is a settlement` `the total can be assessed`

-- Situation: only where the respondent has sued the group member.
@export The respondent has sued me in the Federal Court. Can what I am awarded in the class action be held back until that case is decided (s 33U of the Federal Court of Australia Act 1976)?
GIVEN `the respondent is suing me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the respondent commenced a proceeding in the Federal Court against you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can my award be held back?` `the respondent is suing me` MEANS
    `s 33U -- my award can be stayed` `the respondent is suing me`

@export What is the earliest day the Court can set as the last day for group members to claim from a damages fund (s 33ZA(3)(c) of the Federal Court of Australia Act 1976)? Six months after the day of the order setting up the fund.
GIVEN `the day of the fund order` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the Court make the order setting up the fund (ISO date)?
GIVETH A DATE
`What is the earliest fund claim day?` `the day of the fund order` MEANS
    `s 33ZA(3)(c) -- the earliest claim day` `the day of the fund order`

@export Can I claim my payment out of the class action's damages fund on this day (s 33ZA(3)(c), (4) of the Federal Court of Australia Act 1976)? In time on or before the claim day the order fixed; after it, only if the fund is not yet fully paid out and the Court thinks it just to allow it.
GIVEN `the day of the fund order` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the Court make the order setting up the fund (ISO date)?
      `the claim day` IS A DATE @desc What is the day the order fixed, on or before which group members are to claim (ISO date)?
      `the day I claim` IS A DATE @desc On what day will you (or did you) make your claim (ISO date)?
      `the fund is fully paid out` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the fund already been fully distributed?
      `the Court thinks it just` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a late claim: does the Court think it just to allow it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I claim from the fund?` `the day of the fund order` `the claim day` `the day I claim` `the fund is fully paid out` `the Court thinks it just` MEANS
    `s 33ZA -- I can claim from the fund` `the day of the fund order` `the claim day` `the day I claim` `the fund is fully paid out` `the Court thinks it just`

@export In a class action under the consumer protection laws, am I treated as a party, so the Court can order compensation for me, under s 87(1) of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010 or s 238(1) of the Australian Consumer Law (s 33ZH of the Federal Court of Australia Act 1976)?
GIVEN `I am a group member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a group member in the class action?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Am I a party for consumer law compensation orders?` `I am a group member` MEANS
    `s 33ZH -- I count as a party for consumer law orders` `I am a group member`

§§ `Appeals (s 33ZC(6), Federal Court Rules 2011 rr 1.61, 36.03)`

-- Situation: only after judgment, where the representative party does not appeal.
@export If the representative party does not appeal the class action judgment in time, by when can I, as a group member, appeal for the group (s 33ZC(6) of the Federal Court of Australia Act 1976, Federal Court Rules 2011 rr 1.61, 36.03)? 21 days after the representative's time ends: 28 days after judgment (not counting 24 December to 14 January), or a later date the Court fixed. Extensions of time are not counted.
GIVEN `the day of judgment` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the judgment pronounced or the order made (or leave to appeal granted) (ISO date)?
      `the Court fixed an appeal date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Court fix a date for filing a notice of appeal?
      `the appeal date fixed` IS A DATE @desc If so, what date (ISO date)? Ignored otherwise.
GIVETH A DATE
`By when can I appeal for the group?` `the day of judgment` `the Court fixed an appeal date` `the appeal date fixed` MEANS
    `s 33ZC(6) -- my last day to appeal for the group` `the day of judgment` `the Court fixed an appeal date` `the appeal date fixed`

@export Can I, as a group member, bring an appeal for the whole group on this day because the representative party did not appeal in time (s 33ZC(6) of the Federal Court of Australia Act 1976)? Only in the 21 days after the representative's own time to appeal ends.
GIVEN `the day of judgment` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the judgment pronounced or the order made (or leave to appeal granted) (ISO date)?
      `the Court fixed an appeal date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Court fix a date for filing a notice of appeal?
      `the appeal date fixed` IS A DATE @desc If so, what date (ISO date)? Ignored otherwise.
      `the representative appealed in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the representative party (or sub-group representative) appeal within their time?
      `the day I file` IS A DATE @desc On what day will you file your notice of appeal (ISO date)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I appeal for the group?` `the day of judgment` `the Court fixed an appeal date` `the appeal date fixed` `the representative appealed in time` `the day I file` MEANS
    `s 33ZC(6) -- I can appeal for the group` `the day of judgment` `the Court fixed an appeal date` `the appeal date fixed` `the representative appealed in time` `the day I file`
